{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"ade188a0-8455-4927-8ed3-2ba00f43b93c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented a robust fix for the intermittent **500 Internal Server Error** that occurred on the second story publish.\n\n### Root Cause\n- **DynamoDB numeric type restriction**: The `related` function stored similarity scores as Python `float`s. DynamoDB rejects float values, raising:\n  ```\n  TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n  ```\n- The first publish succeeded because the `similar` list was empty (no existing stories). On subsequent publishes, the list contains similarity scores, triggering the error.\n\n### Fix Implemented\n1. **Added Decimal import** – `from decimal import Decimal`.\n2. **Converted similarity scores to `Decimal`** before inserting them into DynamoDB items.\n3. **Updated sorting** to work with `Decimal` values.\n\nThese changes ensure all numeric values conform to DynamoDB’s requirements, preventing the 500 error on any subsequent publish.\n\n---\n\nThe detailed fix is documented in the code change applied to `src/app.py`. This resolves the issue and makes the publish operation idempotent and reliable.\n","duration_seconds":30.777779,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":11077,"output_tokens":1909,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":72064,"total_tokens":12986}}}
